14:## Security Rubrics
16:### SEC-IV: Input Validation
17:| Score | Criteria |
18:|-------|----------|
19:| 5 | All inputs validated, sanitized, and typed. Allowlist approach used. Schema validation on APIs. |
20:| 4 | Most inputs validated with minor gaps. Edge cases may lack validation. |
21:| 3 | Basic validation present but incomplete. Some injection risks remain. |
22:| 2 | Minimal validation. Clear injection vulnerabilities exist. |
23:| 1 | No input validation. User input flows directly to sensitive operations. |
25:### SEC-AZ: Authorization
26:| Score | Criteria |
27:|-------|----------|
28:| 5 | RBAC/ABAC properly implemented. All routes protected. Least privilege enforced. |
29:| 4 | Authorization present with minor gaps (some routes missing checks). |
30:| 3 | Basic auth checks but inconsistent. Privilege escalation may be possible. |
31:| 2 | Weak authorization. Easy bypass or missing on critical routes. |
32:| 1 | No authorization or completely broken access control. |
34:### SEC-CI: Confidentiality/Integrity
35:| Score | Criteria |
36:|-------|----------|
37:| 5 | Encryption at rest and in transit. Proper key management. Data classified and protected. |
38:| 4 | Good encryption with minor gaps. Some sensitive data handling could improve. |
39:| 3 | Basic encryption but inconsistent. Some data exposure risks. |
40:| 2 | Weak or missing encryption. Sensitive data partially exposed. |
41:| 1 | No encryption. Sensitive data in plaintext. Secrets in code. |
43:### SEC-IN: Injection Prevention
44:| Score | Criteria |
45:|-------|----------|
46:| 5 | Parameterized queries everywhere. No string concatenation in queries. ORM used safely. |
47:| 4 | Mostly safe with minor gaps in edge cases. |
48:| 3 | Mixed usage. Some queries parameterized, others vulnerable. |
49:| 2 | Frequent string concatenation in queries. Clear SQL/NoSQL injection paths. |
50:| 1 | Pervasive injection vulnerabilities. Eval/exec with user input. |
52:### SEC-AV: Availability/Resilience
53:| Score | Criteria |
54:|-------|----------|
55:| 5 | Rate limiting, circuit breakers, graceful degradation. DoS protection in place. |
56:| 4 | Good availability measures with minor gaps. |
